@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# DS41 cost-aware draft length on M5 Ultra
+
+Baseline: 3a8e1743, copied compiled kernels, no native changes. The opt-in `DS41_MTP_COST_POLICY=1` selects 1..4 draft tokens from their cumulative confidences and measured verify cost (plus a fixed 5 ms drafter/loop allowance). Below 1024 context tokens the served acceptance-only policy is retained because front-padded sparse index rows depend on verify width. Copy drafts remain unchanged. Keep the existing cap2 / DSpark k4 / CED / 8192-token chunks / prefix-cache 2 GiB / `DS41_VERIFY_TILE=0` settings.
+
+Method: [EVICT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.00342), adapted to chain proposals and offline cost tables. Policy decisions never use runtime timing or batch scheduling.
+
+Real-context c1/c2 L=2..5 profiles are in curve.jsonl; these are operator profiling data, not served performance. The private server uses a memory-owner gpu-exec lock with 245 GiB RSS/footprint and 840-second watchdogs. HTTP client runs only after startup warm-up.
+
+Initial warm same-server A/B (two 256-token samples each): 8K summary 67.97 -> 74.44; Engram explanation 74.48 -> 78.97; prefill explanation 63.65 -> 73.85 tok/s. Every text is identical. c2 is exact with no material throughput change. HTTP returned no logprobs, so its empty logprob hashes are not evidence. Raw full-vocabulary logits, target hidden taps, and final committed cache hashes agree across L=2..5 and mixed rejection/rollback patterns at real 8K and 128K. Ten CPU policy tests pass.
+
+Validation completed. Exact shape/rollback gates additionally pass at 1,024, 1,032, 2,048 and 4,096 tokens. All 48 HTTP responses (short controls, 8K/128K/512K and 8K c2) retain the same per-prompt text hashes. The HTTP layer did not return requested logprobs; raw logit evidence comes from exact-policy.jsonl and exact-threshold.jsonl.
+
+Warm HTTP decode means across three document questions, two 256-token samples per question and mode:
+
+| Context | Baseline | Cost policy | Change |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| 8K | 68.70 | 75.75 | +10.3% |
+| 128K | 67.99 | 70.57 | +3.8% |
+| 512K | 59.54 | 63.53 | +6.7% |
+
+Rates are client streaming decode tok/s after the first visible token, with an explicitly warmed server. Prefix reuse is intentional for repeated decode samples; no prefill speedup is claimed. c2 per-request mean 41.32 -> 41.47 tok/s is within noise. Short controls remain on the old policy and differ by only 1–2% timing noise. The largest lease was 507 seconds; peak measured footprint 236.67 GiB, RSS 226.83 GiB. No watchdog stops.
+
+Runtime commit: 207c27fb. Enable only with `DS41_MTP_COST_POLICY=1`; 0/default retains the served behavior. No native rebuild. Nothing pushed.
