+{"mode": 0, "rep": 0, "prompt": 0, "ctx": 524288, "c": 1, "tokens": 256, "prompt_tokens": 524314, "ttft_s": 272.3793852920003, "decode_tok_s": 58.64608779279492, "text": "This code implements a DeepSeek V4.1 model port for the oMLX/mlx-vlm runtime, covering model definition, caching, quantization, and inference.\n\n- **Model architecture**: Defines the V4.1 language model with CSA2 sparse attention (sliding window + compressed KV), single-pass mHC (hyper-connections), MoE routing, Engram n-gram lookups, and optional vision encoder (ViT + Aligner).\n- **Custom Metal kernels**: Provides packed FP8/FP4 attention, index scoring, top-k selection, SwiGLU activation quantization, hyper-connection mixing, and vocabulary projection kernels optimized for Apple GPUs.\n- **Caching & state**: Implements `DeepseekV41Cache` for request-local state (window KV, compressed KV, index keys, compressor tails, Engram history) with merge/extract support for batching.\n- **Quantization & conversion**: Includes checkpoint conversion (MXFP repacking), oQ3/oQ4 affine quantization with sensitivity/imatrix calibration, Engram table quantization, and MoE expert offloading with bounded residency.\n- **Inference features**: Supports DSpark MTP speculative decoding, CED prefill skip, Engram SSD offload/prefetch", "text_hash": "d19101a1a0b1582950150c52ba8a566e08ea87ceda84bfb2a16b8e2ddfe65809", "logprobs_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "nlogprobs": 0}
+{"mode": 0, "rep": 0, "prompt": 1, "ctx": 524288, "c": 1, "tokens": 256, "prompt_tokens": 524316, "ttft_s": 2.139622167000198, "decode_tok_s": 58.38361303567512, "text": "The Engram tables are a large, sparse lookup mechanism that injects n-gram-based \"memory\" into the residual stream at a few specific layers. The system is split across three files: `engram.py` (the hashing and the module), `storage.py` (the I/O for the tables), and `loading.py` (wiring it up). Here is the full picture.\n\n## 1. What the tables are\n\nEach Engram layer owns an embedding table (`Engram.embed`) with `engram_num_embeddings[table_index]` rows and `engram_head_dim` columns. These tables are enormous, so they are stored as separate safetensors files (the \"engram\" directory) rather than in the main shard index. `source_engram_tables` in `convert.py` discovers them by looking for keys containing `.engram.embed.` and ending in `.weight`, and records the associated `.scale` key/file.\n\nThe tables are **not** part of the normal weight budget. In `oq.py`, `source_budget` counts them separately (`engram_params`/`engram_bytes`) and quantizes them with a uniform affine group-32 policy, excluded from the", "text_hash": "b4c082876f55a99e0ca99137524ed28116a56beda5e3d5d46a332ced68f3c4c1", "logprobs_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "nlogprobs": 0}
+{"mode": 0, "rep": 0, "prompt": 2, "ctx": 524288, "c": 1, "tokens": 256, "prompt_tokens": 524313, "ttft_s": 2.1650234589997126, "decode_tok_s": 62.17821819598217, "text": "The prefill path for DeepSeek V4.1 in this oMLX port is a single forward pass over the full prompt, driven by `LanguageModel._forward` in `language.py`. Here is the step-by-step flow.\n\n## 1. Entry and cache setup\n\n`Model.__call__` (in `model.py`) first calls `get_input_embeddings`, which either returns the raw token embeddings or, for VL requests, splices vision features into the image spans. It then calls `language_model(...)` with `inputs_embeds` when pixels are present.\n\nInside `LanguageModel._forward`:\n\n- If no cache is supplied, `make_cache()` builds one `DeepseekV41Cache` per layer. Each cache is a 7-slot `ArraysCache` holding: offset, window KV, compressed KV, index K, partial KV, partial gates, and Engram history.\n- The per-layer `compress_ratio` is validated against the config; a legacy `None` ratio is upgraded in place.\n- If Engram layers exist but no token map has been installed, it raises \u2014 the tokenizer-derived compressed map is mandatory.\n- `cache[0].make_mask(...)` produces the attention mask (", "text_hash": "914c1b606d5ecd70b6595b02bd93b0b67a00eed75edae367455c10fd23e7e7a2", "logprobs_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "nlogprobs": 0}
