@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# DS41 sprint 3 follow-up gates
+
+Branch `ds41-sprint3-ds41o`, rebased onto served `1f3137bb`. EVICT already shipped as `b393af8b` + `1f3137bb` (original lane commits `207c27fb` + `be897266`). All remaining HTTP comparisons enable `DS41_MTP_COST_POLICY=1`.
+
+## Shared sparse verification: rejected
+
+Cached-output ablations preserve every input dependency using `mx.depends`. They measure an optimistic elimination bound, not a candidate speedup. Deep caches are synthetic extensions of a real 8K prefill. These figures must not be presented as serving throughput.
+
+| Context | L5 baseline, ms | No attention, ms | Elimination bound |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| 256K | 40.780 | 36.299 | 10.99% |
+| 512K | 43.254 | 38.724 | 10.47% |
+| 1M | 51.712 | 46.924 | 9.26% |
+
+The bounded prototype sorts the union of selected KV rows, decodes each unique packed row once into FP32, and uses a slot map to preserve every query's original 32-slot split and accumulation order. All 12 synthetic cases matched raw output bits, across L2/L5, 256K/1M-equivalent key counts, and three overlap levels. It was slower in every cell, including full overlap. Stop at that speed gate; no model integration or serving claim. See `ssv.jsonl`, `ssv.py`, `ssv_probe.py`.
+
+## Exact indexer top-k: no build
+
+| Phase/context | Eliminating all hooked top-k work |
+|---|---:|
+| Decode 256K | 0.34% |
+| Decode 512K | 0.87% |
+| Decode 1M | 2.28% |
+| 8K prefill chunk at 256K | 1.25% |
+| 8K prefill chunk at 1M | 2.39% |
+
+Every result is below the sprint's 8% build threshold. Decode ablations retained exact output hashes. Prefill ablation outputs are cached only for headroom; this is not a changed prefill implementation. `headroom.py` recorded the 256K samples and then hit a cleanup NameError. `headroom_rest.py` corrects cleanup and completes the remaining contexts. No sample spans that error.
+
+## Decode replay: bounded prototype rejected
+
+Main-thread CPU work was 15.86 / 19.56 / 32.63 ms per L5 forward at 256K / 512K / 1M, so the CPU-cost gate passes. CPU work overlaps GPU work; these values are not potential speedup claims. A whole-forward `mx.compile` probe that supplies all cache arrays as inputs fails on a host evaluation boundary:
+
+```
+ValueError: [eval] Attempting to eval an array during function transformations like compile or vmap is not allowed.
+```
+
+It cannot replay changing cache offsets without more runtime work. No replay change ships. The headroom/replay lease peaked at 234.84 GiB physical footprint and 225.44 GiB RSS, below both 245 GiB guards. See `headroom-rest.jsonl`.
+
+## Tool/copy sources and layered prefill
+
+Tool sources passed the warm gate: 100.85 -> 111.41 mean tok/s (+10.5%), all 62 compared responses identical. See `../ds41_sprint3_sources/README.md`. The original copy path already achieves 408/408 and 405/406 accepted drafts on the two copy-heavy diagnostic requests. Hidden retrieval and schema proposals target tool traffic instead. Instrumented trace timings are never used as serving figures.
+
+The actual-weight q3/g128 row-independence gate passed at 512+512 and 8192+8192 rows for both expert input and output projections; the 8K comparison also passed a raw-bit check. Grouping the input projection saved only 4.35% (27.877 -> 26.663 ms for two chunks), while grouping the output projection regressed 60.8% (29.600 -> 47.599 ms). These are operator diagnostics, not serving figures. Drop layered prefill before scheduler work; see `rows-speed.jsonl`. Peak footprint 9.56 GiB.
+
+## Carryover drafting
+
+Feasibility only; see `CARRYOVER.md`. No training was requested or started.
