+# Pipe1 run 3: step numerics fixed; handoff to Opus
+
+2026-09-25. The COORDINATOR 11:26 note directs a clean handoff to Opus.
+The invalid 8 ms latency gate is withdrawn. Step numerics now pass; the
+cross-backend gate is still failing, so original pipeline serving is not ready.
+No c1/c2 end-to-end decode or quality figures are claimed.
+
+## Numerical result
+
+`pipe1-run3-gate-result.json` records 21 strict TCP/CUDA-graph cases:
+prefixes 256, 8190 and 8192; L1–5; reject three speculative rows while keeping
+two, then L4; subsequent L1. All h19, pre, layer-20 KV and index comparisons
+have relative RMS **0.0**, maximum absolute difference **0.0**, and packed
+KV/index bytes are **100% equal** to full prefill of the same token sequence.
+This covers the 8192 page/chunk boundary. Prior run-2 h19 RMS was
+0.053–0.111, rising to 0.249–0.409 after rollback.
+
+Both prefill and step in the phase-3 engine use the corrected arithmetic;
+the checkpoint weights are unchanged. The original phase-2 launcher does
+not install these arithmetic hooks and remains independently restorable.
+
+The fixes in `hooks/split_nv/consistent.py` are:
+
+- Sort decode indexer top-k by logical position, matching prefill. Unordered
+  atomic emission had made repeats and rollback diverge nondeterministically.
+- Use the same FlashInfer prefill attention kernel for every batch width.
+  For <=64 rows, masked dummy queries select that kernel; they have no keys.
+  Decode's split-K arithmetic rounded differently from prefill.
+- Use a fixed-reduction Triton BF16/FP32 projection for router logits,
+  compressor projections (including layer-20 ratio 1), and indexer projections.
+  Tiny GEMV versus cuBLAS reductions initially differed at about 1e-7 in router
+  logits; quantization amplified that into substantial hidden-state drift.
+- Execute one-row steps with W2. The dummy row's cache/ring location is zero;
+  only real tokens enter Engram history. This avoids remaining one-row kernels.
+
+Earlier fixes remain: ratio-2 ring size 16; per-width graph metadata;
+int64 allocator/prefix indices; bounded lazy Engram rollback/commit.
+
+## Warm step measurements
+
+8,213 cached tokens from `ref/ids-8192.json`, 16 repetitions per width,
+first two discarded, median of 14 warm samples. Original FP4/FP8 encoder,
+TP2 RTX PRO 6000 pair, pinned Engram copy, graphs W2–5. No model load,
+JIT, graph capture or prefill time is included.
+
+| Rows | Prior box ms (numerically failing) | Corrected box ms from Mac | Mac RTT ms |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| 1 | 9.422 | 12.971 | 14.314 |
+| 2 | 9.872 | 12.836 | 14.697 |
+| 3 | 10.450 | 13.407 | 15.200 |
+| 4 | 11.062 | 13.915 | 15.339 |
+| 5 | 11.219 | 14.101 | 15.725 |
+
+RTT minus box includes input preparation, queueing, copies/packing and both
+network hops. These are encoder timings, not end-to-end decode speed.
+The coordinator withdrew the 8 ms gate; these box steps remain below the
+reported Mac verify time of 27–37 ms.
+
+## Cross-backend status and next work
+
+Still blocked by arithmetic differences, not checkpoint precision:
+existing original Mac reference versus corrected CUDA, rows 8205–8212,
+h19 cosine **0.97197797**, relative RMS **0.23748192**. The target is cosine
+>=0.995 on the 8K fixture. The earlier full 256-row comparison was 0.9664;
+the new eight-row figure is a different slice and is not a claimed improvement.
+`pipe1-run3-cross-result.json` records the current CPU comparison.
+
+Artifacts:
+
+- CUDA selected-row trace: `/mnt/nvme-2/pipe1-cuda-trace-8213.pt` (25 MiB).
+  `SPLIT_NV_TRACE=1` enables the opt-in hooks and writes
+  `/dev/shm/split-nv/cuda-trace-8213.pt` when prefix length is 8213.
+- Existing original Mac boundary: `/mnt/nvme-2/native-encoder-8k.safetensors`;
+  Mac original at `~/llm/ds41/split1/native-encoder-8k.safetensors`.
+- CPU comparator: `tools/compare_cross.py --cuda-trace <trace>`; optional
+  `--mac-trace <safetensors>` compares common layer/subcomponent keys.
+- Prepared Mac trace: `benchmarks/pipe1/trace_encoder.py` on ds41-pipe1.
+  It uses split1's successful reference tree `~/src/wt/ds41-split-wire`
+  (`PIPE1_TRACE_TREE` overrides). Its first launch mistakenly used pipe1's tree,
+  which lacks encoder_export; it exited **before model load**. The import root
+  is corrected and syntax checked, but the probe was not rerun after the stop
+  directive. Its 245 GiB/840 s watchdog and inherited gpu-exec lock are required.
+
+Localize with the prepared Mac trace first. Source inspection found two
+specific candidates, **not yet experimentally proven** as the dominant cause:
+FlashInfer quantizes Q/attention probabilities and requantizes compressed FP4
+KV into its FP8 cache; Mac attention consumes its published packed formats.
+Also inspect routed expert weighting: Mac applies route weights before
+activation quantization/down projection, whereas the inspected FlashInfer
+path passes token_final_scales to finalization. The existing SGLang Triton
+attention backend offers an experiment without writing a new kernel.
+
+After cosine passes: complete original decoder integration (load/replay smoke
+preserved at Mac commit 98787451), recheck step numerics if arithmetic changes,
+then warm c1/c2 decode at 8K/128K/512K with box/link/Mac/draft breakdown, then
+split1's pipeline quality harness. Mac teacher forcing now explicitly uses
+verify=True, fixed L4/EOS-1 padding as required by that harness. That one-line
+correction is not an end-to-end quality validation.
+
+## Reproduction and operational state
+
+Announce every swap in `~/llm/ds41/PROGRESS.md` on m5 before running:
+
+```sh
+cd /home/ian/split-nv
+SPLIT_NV_TRACE=1 python3 tools/pipe1_gate.py <unique-label> \
+  --graphs 2,3,4,5 --experiment-seconds 480 --restore-seconds 330
+```
+
+The gate validates all three prefixes, times box and Mac TCP, then restores
+`run_encoder.sh` in a finally block, checking `/health` and a real `/v1/prefill`.
+This budget plus stop margin is <=14 minutes. Root must have >=100 GiB free;
+both launchers retain `--ulimit core=0`. Diagnostic eager isolation is
+`--selftest numerics --graphs ''` (it deliberately bypasses automatic
+consistent.py installation and applies its named experiments explicitly).
+
+Final window7 restored phase 2 after 308.50 s (see driver receipt for exact
+value): health up and real 441592-byte prefill. Root >226 GiB free.
+Mac served q3 reloaded and replied "Ready."; only its memory-owning PID holds
+the Mac lock. No pipe1 Mac model or phase-3 engine remains running.
+
+Keep serving phase 2 with `run_encoder.sh` + existing host server.py on
+10.10.10.1:10051, ENGRAM_PINNED=copy, TP2. Mac served tree remains bd94a080,
+DS41_MTP_COST_POLICY=1 and DS41_EXTRA_DRAFT=1. Phase-3 experimental defaults
+are run_engine.sh, graphs 2,3,4,5, original encoder checkpoint and original
+Mac half at `~/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-pipe1-mlx`; do not treat them as
+an accepted original-model serving configuration yet. Nothing was pushed.
